---Represents a textual expression in the Common Expression Language (CEL) syntax. CEL is a C-like expression language. The syntax and semantics of CEL are documented at https://github.com/google/cel-spec. Example (Comparison): title: "Summary size limit" description: "Determines if a summary is less than 100 chars" expression: "document.summary.size() < 100" Example (Equality): title: "Requestor is owner" description: "Determines if requestor is the document owner" expression: "document.owner == request.auth.claims.email" Example (Logic): title: "Public documents" description: "Determine whether the document should be publicly visible" expression: "document.type != 'private' && document.type != 'internal'" Example (Data Manipulation): title: "Notification string" description: "Create a notification string with a timestamp." expression: "'New message received at ' + string(document.create_time)" The exact variables and functions that may be referenced within an expression are determined by the service that evaluates it. See the service documentation for additional information.
---@class gcp.vmwareengine_v1.Expr
---@field description? string Optional. Description of the expression. This is a longer text which describes the expression, e.g. when hovered over it in a UI.
---@field expression? string Textual representation of an expression in Common Expression Language syntax.
---@field location? string Optional. String indicating the location of the expression for error reporting, e.g. a file name and a position in the file.
---@field title? string Optional. Title for the expression, i.e. a short string describing its purpose. This can be used e.g. in UIs which allow to enter the expression.

---External access firewall rules for filtering incoming traffic destined to `ExternalAddress` resources.
---@class gcp.vmwareengine_v1.ExternalAccessRule
---@field sourceIpRanges? gcp.vmwareengine_v1.IpRangeList If source ranges are specified, the external access rule applies only to traffic that has a source IP address in these ranges. These ranges can either be expressed in the CIDR format or as an IP address. As only inbound rules are supported, `ExternalAddress` resources cannot be the source IP addresses of an external access rule. To match all source addresses, specify `0.0.0.0/0`.
---@field description? string User-provided description for this external access rule.
---@field priority? number External access rule priority, which determines the external access rule to use when multiple rules apply. If multiple rules have the same priority, their ordering is non-deterministic. If specific ordering is required, assign unique priorities to enforce such ordering. The external access rule priority is an integer from 100 to 4096, both inclusive. Lower integers indicate higher precedence. For example, a rule with priority `100` has higher precedence than a rule with priority `101`.
---@field sourcePorts? gcp.vmwareengine_v1.StringList A list of source ports to which the external access rule applies. This field is only applicable for the UDP or TCP protocol. Each entry must be either an integer or a range. For example: `["22"]`, `["80","443"]`, or `["12345-12349"]`. To match all source ports, specify `["0-65535"]`.
---@field name? string Output only. The resource name of this external access rule. Resource names are schemeless URIs that follow the conventions in https://cloud.google.com/apis/design/resource_names. For example: `projects/my-project/locations/us-central1/networkPolicies/my-policy/externalAccessRules/my-rule`
---@field ipProtocol? string The IP protocol to which the external access rule applies. This value can be one of the following three protocol strings (not case-sensitive): `tcp`, `udp`, or `icmp`.
---@field action? gcp.vmwareengine_v1.ExternalAccessRuleActionEnum The action that the external access rule performs.
---@field state? gcp.vmwareengine_v1.ExternalAccessRuleStateEnum Output only. The state of the resource.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Creation time of this resource.
---@field destinationPorts? gcp.vmwareengine_v1.StringList A list of destination ports to which the external access rule applies. This field is only applicable for the UDP or TCP protocol. Each entry must be either an integer or a range. For example: `["22"]`, `["80","443"]`, or `["12345-12349"]`. To match all destination ports, specify `["0-65535"]`.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Last update time of this resource.
---@field uid? string Output only. System-generated unique identifier for the resource.
---@field destinationIpRanges? gcp.vmwareengine_v1.IpRangeList If destination ranges are specified, the external access rule applies only to the traffic that has a destination IP address in these ranges. The specified IP addresses must have reserved external IP addresses in the scope of the parent network policy. To match all external IP addresses in the scope of the parent network policy, specify `0.0.0.0/0`. To match a specific external IP address, specify it using the `IpRange.external_address` property.

---@alias gcp.vmwareengine_v1.ExternalAccessRuleActionEnum "ACTION_UNSPECIFIED"|"ALLOW"|"DENY"

